to get married,

35
00:02:09,693 --> 00:02:11,946
and what did you do
when your sister got the money?

36
00:02:12,071 --> 00:02:14,573
You ended up divorced. [laughs mockingly]

37
00:02:14,698 --> 00:02:19,078
-What a pathetic loser. [laughs]
-Why are you bringing that up again?

38
00:02:19,203 --> 00:02:21,580
People are gonna think
you bought me a house or something.

39
00:02:21,705 --> 00:02:23,415
You only gave me
a measly five million won.

40
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:26,752
[gasps] "Measly five million"? Hey!

41
00:02:26,877 --> 00:02:29,338
-[funky music playing]
-There's a huge difference

42
00:02:29,463 --> 00:02:31,840
between someone with 100 million
lending you five million

43
00:02:31,966 --> 00:02:34,301
and someone with ten million
doing the same. Stop it!

44
00:02:34,426 --> 00:02:36,887
And if someone like your sister
only has five and a half

45
00:02:37,012 --> 00:02:39,014
and lends you five,
you seriously don't get it?

46
00:02:39,598 --> 00:02:41,350
What I took isn't even close!

47
00:02:41,976 --> 00:02:45,521
Never mind I handed you
all that I had, okay?

48
00:02:47,356 --> 00:02:50,317
That five million won
wasn't just five million.

49
00:02:50,985 --> 00:02:54,989
It was all I had then, you know?
It'd be equal to 500 million.

50
00:02:55,114 --> 00:02:58,033
You have no right to use
the word "measly" in that context, got it?

51
00:02:58,158 --> 00:03:00,744
And didn't I pay you back, huh?
Every last won.

52
00:03:00,869 --> 00:03:04,331
God, did you even hear
a word I just said, huh?

53
00:03:04,456 --> 00:03:07,209
If five million was worth 500,

54
00:03:07,334 --> 00:03:09,753
then you should've gave me 500 million,

55
00:03:09,878 --> 00:03:11,422
-you idiot!
-You loan shark!

56
00:03:11,547 --> 00:03:13,007
Yeah, sure, I'm a loan shark,
but you're a dumbass!

57
00:03:13,132 --> 00:03:15,175
-You're scamming your own brother?
-Just stop it already!

58
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:18,554
-[sighs] Mm…
-[sighs]

59
