SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT

154
00:09:18,330 --> 00:09:19,956
Are you married, Counselor?

155
00:09:21,416 --> 00:09:22,667
Why do you ask?

156
00:09:28,507 --> 00:09:31,009
-So, it wasn't this idiot.
-"This idiot"?

157
00:09:31,134 --> 00:09:33,678
[indistinct chatter]

158
00:09:33,804 --> 00:09:36,723
[pen scrawling]

159
00:09:42,687 --> 00:09:44,356
[sighs deeply]

160
00:09:47,275 --> 00:09:49,111
[Mi-do]  Show up like this again,
and you're dead.

161
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:50,904
[scoffs]

162
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:53,365
[music stops]

163
00:09:54,116 --> 00:09:55,200
[door opens]

164
00:09:56,034 --> 00:09:58,537
[Tae-seung] Is it because your mom owns
a building in Yeonhui-dong?

165
00:09:59,913 --> 00:10:01,998
Wow, you are something else.

166
00:10:05,961 --> 00:10:08,755
Well, I need to know who I'm dealing with.

167
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:12,467
In this business, we call it
a background check or due diligence.

168
00:10:13,969 --> 00:10:16,805
Your oldest brother owns
a drain cleaning company.

169
00:10:16,930 --> 00:10:19,349
The youngest was
the first Korean free diver

170
00:10:19,474 --> 00:10:21,768
to set a national record
in constant weight.

171
00:10:21,893 --> 00:10:23,937
And your longtime boyfriend…

172
00:10:26,106 --> 00:10:27,691
Oh, you guys just broke up.

173
00:10:30,068 --> 00:10:33,280
[gasps] Was it because he found out?

174
00:10:33,405 --> 00:10:37,576
[sighs] Wow, that scumbag.

175
00:10:38,243 --> 00:10:39,995
Piece of shit, honestly.

176
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:43,999
You don't abandon a girl
at her lowest, right?

177
00:10:47,669 --> 00:10:49,880
[Tae-seung over recording]
Well, I need to know who I'm dealing with.

178
00:10:50,005 --> 00:10:51,631
-[quirky music playing]
-[Tae-seung]  In this business,

179
00:10:51,756 --> 00:10:55,051
we call it a background check
or due diligence.

180
00:10:55,177 --> 00:10:58,013
Your oldest brother owns
a drain cleaning com--

181
00:10:59,097 --> 00:11:01,558
Unauthorized background check
on a civilian.

182
00:11:01,683 --> 00:11:03,435
Illegal interference in a mediation.

183
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:07,689
Threats made against a family.
Inciting fear under the guise of a deal.

184
00:11:07,814 --> 00:11:10,233
This will help in court, right?
Well, thanks.

185
00:11:11,568 --> 00:11:13,945
Let's add one more to that.
Property damage.

186
00:11:16,156 --> 00:11:18,492
-[grunts]
-[cell phone crunching]

187
00:11:21,369 --> 00:11:22,204
[exhales]

188
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:27,167
[sighs]

189
00:11:28,919 --> 00:11:32,047
Well, I'll buy you a new phone
and send it to you today.

190
00:11:34,049 --> 00:11:35,383
[music concludes]

191
00:11:35,926 --> 00:11:37,677
[sighs] Hmm.

192
00:11:37,802 --> 00:11:42,974
[exhales] Listen…
I'm really busy with work lately,

193
00:11:44,059 --> 00:11:46,436
so I wanted to settle this trivial case
and be done,

194
00:11:46,561 --> 00:11:48,522
which is why I was being nice to you.

195
00:11:48,647 --> 00:11:51,274
[scoffs] And you're making this difficult.

196
00:11:51,942 --> 00:11:54,069
Since you want it so badly,
I'll see you in court.

197
00:11:54,194 --> 00:11:55,570
I really hope you're ready.

198
00:12:02,994 --> 00:12:04,329
-[Mi-do grunts]
-[gasps]

199
00:12:05,372 --> 00:12:10,544
-[quirky instrumental music playing]
-[breathes heavily]

200
00:12:10,669 --> 00:12:11,628
[gasps softly]

201
00:12:13,672 --> 00:12:15,006
Send me the bill.

202
00:12:15,131 --> 00:12:18,260
[panting] Oh, and make sure
to get the latest model.

203
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:21,721
A white phone with one tera of storage.

204
00:12:28,770 --> 00:12:29,980
[music concludes]

205
00:12:30,105 --> 00:12:32,566
[indistinct chatter]

206
00:12:42,450 --> 00:12:45,245
[Su-a]  I know the reason
there was an issue with the fourth sample.

207
00:12:45,370 --> 00:12:48,582
-If you want to know, I can tell you.
-[light instrumental music playing]

208
00:12:53,169 --> 00:12:55,922
On the 9th at noon,
over a bowl of Pyongyang  naengmyeon.

209
00:12:57,299 --> 00:12:58,425
I'll be waiting there.

210
00:12:58,550 --> 00:13:01,136
[inhales deeply] Uh, um…

211
00:13:03,722 --> 00:13:06,266
[groans, grunts] Damn it!

212
00:13:07,601 --> 00:13:10,812
-Huh? Huh? Why are you here?
-[sighs]

213
00:13:10,937 --> 00:13:14,733
Ah, jeez, you're so impatient.
Is it because of the sample schedule?

214
00:13:15,442 --> 00:13:18,528
[grunts playfully] Gotcha.

215
00:13:18,653 --> 00:13:20,363
-[Namgung] Can you talk?
-[Ho-sik] Huh?

216
00:13:20,488 --> 00:13:21,656
[Namgung] Come on, let's have a chat.

217
00:13:22,907 --> 00:13:24,826
[Su-a] I guess you forgot our plans today.

218
00:13:25,994 --> 00:13:27,704
[music concludes]

219
00:13:27,829 --> 00:13:29,080
Ah.

220
00:13:31,416 --> 00:13:34,461
I never really said
that I was gonna be there, did I?

221
00:13:35,879 --> 00:13:39,424
Well, no. But there was a difference
between the lab and factory samples.

222
00:13:39,549 --> 00:13:40,925
I heard you were curious about it.

223
00:13:41,051 --> 00:13:43,803
You visited the farms
asking questions, didn't you?

224
00:13:43,928 --> 00:13:46,014
I did. You're right.

225
00:13:46,723 --> 00:13:51,394
But let's just say I don't have the fire
to dive into sticky situations. Hmm.

226
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:54,898
I look young,
but I'm 35, you know. [chuckles softly]

227
00:13:55,023 --> 00:13:57,359
Hmm. Is that the actual reason?

228
00:13:57,484 --> 00:14:00,779
Of course. After the age of 35,
you start losing muscle mass.

229
00:14:00,904 --> 00:14:03,281
And you're considered too old
to get job subsidies

230
00:14:03,406 --> 00:14:04,741
or national allowance.

231
00:14:04,866 --> 00:14:07,661
It'd be wise
to start taking good care of myself.

232
00:14:07,786 --> 00:14:10,163
Basically, stay out of trouble.

233
00:14:10,830 --> 00:14:13,917
I want to work here,
avoiding trouble until I retire.

234
00:14:14,668 --> 00:14:16,002
That's the reason.

235
00:14:18,213 --> 00:14:20,757
We're producing
with imported sweet potatoes too.

236
00:14:21,299 --> 00:14:23,718
[whimsical instrumental music playing]

237
00:14:24,761 --> 00:14:25,804
[inhales sharply]

238
00:14:26,596 --> 00:14:27,972
I'll pretend you never said that.

239
00:14:28,682 --> 00:14:30,225
I did say it.

240
00:14:34,312 --> 00:14:35,397
And I never heard it.

241
00:14:36,356 --> 00:14:37,440
[inhales deeply]

242
00:14:40,443 --> 00:14:41,736
Of course, I apologize.

243
00:14:42,529 --> 00:14:44,614
I guess I'm asking
too much of the wrong person.

244
00:14:45,699 --> 00:14:46,866
I see what you mean.

245
00:14:52,372 --> 00:14:53,456
[exhales sharply]

246
00:14:54,541 --> 00:14:57,502
[Su-a] The Hatguma Chips?
Texture is bad too.

247
00:14:57,627 --> 00:15:02,090
Especially the sweet and spicy combo.
Absolutely disgusting batch.

248
00:15:10,890 --> 00:15:11,933
[exhales sharply]

249
00:15:13,977 --> 00:15:16,062
-[music fades]
-By the way, Mr. Yoon asked me

250
00:15:16,187 --> 00:15:18,773
to send over the bidding plan
first thing tomorrow.

251
00:15:18,898 --> 00:15:21,192
-Really?
-Someone broke into his house.

252
00:15:21,317 --> 00:15:23,695
He's going to the police.
He said they forced the lock.

253
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:25,864
-For real?
-[Sang-hun] Yeah.

254
00:15:26,823 --> 00:15:27,949
[door closes]

255
00:15:28,074 --> 00:15:30,660
[door lock beeping]

256
00:15:30,785 --> 00:15:32,579
-[Namgung sighs]
-[funky instrumental music playing]

257
00:15:33,288 --> 00:15:37,125
[card machine beeps]

258
00:15:37,250 --> 00:15:39,294
[customer] Doesn't work?
Is the machine broken?

259
00:15:39,419 --> 00:15:42,714
[owner] Oh, why would it be broken?
It worked fine earlier.

260
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:47,260
-[alarm beeping]
-[Sang-hun] Dang it.

261
00:15:47,969 --> 00:15:49,637
-What's wrong with it?
-[alarm beeping]

262
00:15:51,014 --> 00:15:53,224
-[alarm beeping]
-[Sang-hun] Oh, shoot.

263
00:15:53,933 --> 00:15:55,351
[alarm beeping]

264
00:15:57,061 --> 00:16:03,777
[car alarm honking]

265
00:16:03,902 --> 00:16:07,739
[car alarm honking echoes]

266
00:16:10,074 --> 00:16:12,202
-[scanner alarm beeping]
-[sighs]

267
00:16:14,037 --> 00:16:15,497
Not again. Dang it.

268
00:16:17,499 --> 00:16:20,877
[scanner alarm continues beeping]

269
00:16:21,002 --> 00:16:23,671
-[Sang-hun] Seriously?
-Hey!

270
00:16:23,797 --> 00:16:26,466
-[dramatic musical sting]
-[gulps]

271
00:16:26,591 --> 00:16:28,510
Didn't I tell you to fix that thing?

272
00:16:28,635 --> 00:16:30,553
-[funky instrumental music continues]
-You didn't, sir.

273
00:16:30,678 --> 00:16:34,182
I told you many times in my head.
Go fix that now.

274
00:16:35,517 --> 00:16:37,852
[music concludes]

275
00:16:47,403 --> 00:16:50,824
[inhales deeply, sighs]

276
00:17:03,503 --> 00:17:07,465
[sentimental piano music playing]

277
00:17:44,752 --> 00:17:45,712
Wait…

278
00:18:08,109 --> 00:18:09,027
HONDURAS KARAOKE

279
00:18:09,152 --> 00:18:11,321
-[dramatic pop music playing]
-[Mi-do, in Korean]  ♪ I pushed you away ♪

280
00:18:11,446 --> 00:18:15,575
♪ Only after love has left ♪

281
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:19,704
♪ Do we realize? ♪

282
00:18:20,246 --> 00:18:25,501
♪ Why did I wander
When you were right beside me? ♪

283
00:18:25,627 --> 00:18:30,256
♪ Now I finally know the… ♪

284
00:18:30,381 --> 00:18:33,301
-[music stops]
-[in English] Ah, shit. [sighs]

285
00:18:34,802 --> 00:18:36,596
Listen, I thought it through.

286
00:18:37,347 --> 00:18:41,768
If you and Namgung are breaking up,
I think I should take his side.

287
00:18:41,893 --> 00:18:42,769
Mm-hmm, right?

288
00:18:45,146 --> 00:18:47,649
You traitor.

289
00:18:48,191 --> 00:18:50,902
-[groans, sighs]
-You'd think Namgung birthed him,

290
00:18:51,027 --> 00:18:52,320
like he's his son.

291
00:18:53,821 --> 00:18:58,034
Yeah, he kind of is.
They've known each other since he was two.

292
00:18:58,159 --> 00:18:59,285
[can lid pops]

293
00:19:07,210 --> 00:19:10,630
I'm really done with Namgung.
I won't see him again.

294
00:19:13,925 --> 00:19:15,802
And I don't need your pity
so you can stop.

295
00:19:15,927 --> 00:19:18,805
Listen here. Don't flatter yourself.

296
00:19:18,930 --> 00:19:20,306
I'm not here as your friend.

297
00:19:20,431 --> 00:19:22,517
-I'm here as a producer.
-[scoffs]

298
00:19:22,642 --> 00:19:25,019
[Yeon-ju] I came here to talk you
into accepting the settlement,

299
00:19:25,144 --> 00:19:27,689
but I can see you're in no state
to discuss this.

300
00:19:28,398 --> 00:19:31,693
Good luck with the lawsuit.
We'll do what we can.

301
00:19:37,657 --> 00:19:42,370
And this isn't as your friend or producer,
but just as a fellow human being…

302
00:19:42,495 --> 00:19:43,663
Mm-mm, save it.

303
00:19:43,788 --> 00:19:46,082
Please go back to Namgung,
for your own good.

304
00:19:52,088 --> 00:19:53,297
[poignant piano music playing]

305
00:19:53,423 --> 00:19:56,259
I'm never getting back together with him.

306
00:19:59,554 --> 00:20:01,472
I don't want to hate him anymore.

307
00:20:04,183 --> 00:20:06,352
And I don't want to be hated either.

308
00:20:08,271 --> 00:20:09,230
Hmm.

309
00:20:11,149 --> 00:20:12,191
[chuckles softly]

310
00:20:13,609 --> 00:20:14,986
[gulps]

311
00:20:19,991 --> 00:20:22,368
[door lock beeps]

312
00:20:27,457 --> 00:20:29,000
She's so lazy.

313
00:20:31,127 --> 00:20:32,962
[door lock chimes]

314
00:20:38,885 --> 00:20:39,761
[door lock beeps]

315
00:20:39,886 --> 00:20:43,264
-[wind chimes tinkling]
-[sighs]

316
00:20:44,432 --> 00:20:45,391
[sighs]

317
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:49,896
She doesn't even care about the fine dust.

318
00:20:51,189 --> 00:20:52,315
[music fades]

319
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,399
[sighs]

320
00:21:00,948 --> 00:21:03,159
[sighs] She should really clean up.

321
00:21:08,748 --> 00:21:10,708
Jeez, how can she live like this?

322
00:21:15,004 --> 00:21:17,173
She didn't do her laundry.

323
00:21:24,430 --> 00:21:25,473
[inhales sharply]

324
00:21:27,850 --> 00:21:28,768
[sighs]

325
00:21:30,978 --> 00:21:35,233
-[chuckles softly]
-[whimsical piano music playing]

326
00:21:35,358 --> 00:21:36,442
Oh, shit.

327
00:21:38,528 --> 00:21:41,030
[panting] Really now, bro?

328
00:21:50,456 --> 00:21:54,752
-[cups clinking]
-[keypad beeping]

329
00:21:54,877 --> 00:21:55,837
[gasps]

330
00:21:57,130 --> 00:22:02,385
[mutters, groans]

331
00:22:04,554 --> 00:22:05,429
Um…

332
00:22:07,181 --> 00:22:08,808
-Hello.
-Hmm…

333
00:22:09,892 --> 00:22:11,018
[music concludes]

334
00:22:11,144 --> 00:22:13,729
-Hey, my charger.
-[exhales]

335
00:22:13,855 --> 00:22:16,732
We broke up
and I want my stuff back, you know?

336
00:22:16,858 --> 00:22:19,861
-[quirky instrumental music playing]
-[jacket unzipping]

337
00:22:21,404 --> 00:22:24,407
[mutters, grunts]

338
00:22:25,741 --> 00:22:26,909
[groans]

339
00:22:31,372 --> 00:22:33,499
-[music fades]
-[grunts, groans]

340
00:22:39,505 --> 00:22:41,465
[groans]

341
00:22:43,509 --> 00:22:47,054
[groans]

342
00:22:48,681 --> 00:22:50,266
[groans]

343
00:22:51,642 --> 00:22:57,273
[tender guitar music playing]

344
00:22:58,357 --> 00:23:01,611
[whimpers, sobs]

345
00:23:02,737 --> 00:23:05,072
[sniffles, whimpers]

346
00:23:07,867 --> 00:23:08,910
[sobs]

347
00:23:09,619 --> 00:23:13,080
Uncle… [sniffles] …you're such a jerk.

348
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:16,626
[sobs, whimpers]

349
00:23:19,503 --> 00:23:23,883
[sniffles, sobs]

350
00:23:24,008 --> 00:23:27,220
[mutters]

351
00:23:29,055 --> 00:23:30,139
[whimpers]

352
00:23:31,766 --> 00:23:32,892
[groans softly]

353
00:23:37,230 --> 00:23:38,689
[exhales]

354
00:23:39,315 --> 00:23:40,358
[sighs]

355
00:23:41,776 --> 00:23:44,820
SEO JU-HYEOK

356
00:23:44,946 --> 00:23:48,658
-[music fades]
-[cell phone ringing]

357
00:23:51,577 --> 00:23:53,037
Ju-hyeok, listen, you can't just--

358
00:23:53,162 --> 00:23:54,497
[Tae-seung over cell phone]  Song Hae-na.

359
00:23:56,332 --> 00:23:57,959
Han Tae-seung? You have his phone?

360
00:23:58,084 --> 00:23:58,918
SONG HAE-NA

361
00:23:59,043 --> 00:24:01,254
[Hae-na]  I wanna talk
to Ju-hyeok one last time.

362
00:24:01,837 --> 00:24:05,216
-Please, I really need to.
-No, you can't. I'm sorry.

363
00:24:08,511 --> 00:24:12,807
And I'm going to have to ask you
to stop confusing the genres.

364
00:24:13,641 --> 00:24:18,020
You're in a soap opera, yet you're acting
like it's a romance. [scoffs]

365
00:24:19,563 --> 00:24:22,775
-It's kind of sad.
-You're not getting away with this.

366
00:24:23,901 --> 00:24:26,779
I will stop you from doing this.

367
00:24:26,904 --> 00:24:30,533
All I ask is that you don't get
your revenge on a Thursday or Friday.

368
00:24:31,575 --> 00:24:34,745
I have a couple of meetings.
Good talking to you.

369
00:24:36,706 --> 00:24:38,082
[exhales deeply]

370
00:24:38,207 --> 00:24:40,167
[tense music playing]

371
00:24:40,293 --> 00:24:41,544
[sighs]

372
00:24:42,128 --> 00:24:43,045
JAEKANG LAW FIRM

373
00:24:43,170 --> 00:24:45,673
[cell phone ringing]

374
00:24:45,798 --> 00:24:47,550
[automated voice]
The person you are calling is unavailable.

375
00:24:47,675 --> 00:24:50,219
-Please leave your message.
-[inhales deeply, sighs]

376
00:24:59,103 --> 00:25:01,731
Ju-hyeok,
I'm not a little girl. [chuckles]

377
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:05,401
Don't worry about me.
You're doing business. [chuckles]

378
00:25:05,943 --> 00:25:08,279
Just wrap up your work
and I'll see you soon.

379
00:25:09,572 --> 00:25:11,115
[chuckles] I love you.

380
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:12,825
-[grunts]
-[lipstick clattering]

381
00:25:14,618 --> 00:25:15,995
That color doesn't suit you.

382
00:25:16,120 --> 00:25:18,456
[tense music continues]

383
00:25:24,712 --> 00:25:26,130
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

384
00:25:26,255 --> 00:25:27,923
Oh, shit.

385
00:25:30,259 --> 00:25:32,803
[cell phone vibrating]

386
00:25:32,928 --> 00:25:34,305
ACTRESS SONG HAE-NA

387
00:25:34,430 --> 00:25:36,515
[music intensifies]

388
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:38,100
Where the hell are you, huh?

389
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:41,020
Is this a joke?

390
00:25:41,145 --> 00:25:44,357
[Hae-na]  I slipped something fun
into Kang Ji-yeon's bag earlier.

391
00:25:45,107 --> 00:25:47,777
Pictures of Ju-hyeok and me at the hotel.

392
00:25:48,402 --> 00:25:51,447
-Hmm. Funny, isn't it?
-[sighs]

393
00:25:52,198 --> 00:25:53,324
Ms. Song…

394
00:25:54,950 --> 00:25:58,037
-stop doing things you'll regret.
-I'm curious.

395
00:25:59,163 --> 00:26:03,542
I wonder how well Seo Ju-hyeok's dog
can clean up his mess.

396
00:26:07,046 --> 00:26:10,049
[inhales sharply, sighs]

397
00:26:12,009 --> 00:26:14,845
-[sighs]
-[cell phone vibrates]

398
00:26:19,558 --> 00:26:21,769
[dramatic musical sting]

399
00:26:22,728 --> 00:26:24,772
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO

400
00:26:27,608 --> 00:26:29,360
[music fades]

401
00:26:31,320 --> 00:26:34,782
-You're awfully quiet.
-It's how I think.

402
00:26:34,907 --> 00:26:35,866
[chuckles softly]

403
00:26:35,991 --> 00:26:37,243
[inhales deeply]

404
00:26:37,368 --> 00:26:39,620
By the way,
the pictures are already in the cloud.

405
00:26:40,496 --> 00:26:42,873
Whatever you're thinking,
don't get any ideas.

406
00:26:47,545 --> 00:26:48,838
Stop talking down to me.

407
00:26:50,506 --> 00:26:52,675
One perk of a power trip is doing that.

408
00:26:54,468 --> 00:26:57,096
-[chuckles]
-[sighs]

409
00:26:57,805 --> 00:27:00,057
Tell me what happened. I need to know.

410
00:27:00,850 --> 00:27:03,561
She spent three months
in production together.

411
00:27:03,686 --> 00:27:05,855
That color doesn't suit you.

412
00:27:06,814 --> 00:27:10,317
[Mi-do]  Even hidden under a scarf and hat,
I recognized her right away.

413
00:27:10,443 --> 00:27:13,320
[intriguing piano music playing]

414
00:27:15,322 --> 00:27:19,785
-[laughs] You know… Oh!
-Oh, no. I'm sorry. I'm such an idiot.

415
00:27:19,910 --> 00:27:22,913
-Oh. [pants] Oh, forgive me.
-Don't worry. I'll do it. Give me some…

416
00:27:23,038 --> 00:27:24,790
-[Mi-do] Gosh.
-[Ji-yeon] Do you have any napkins?

417
00:27:25,791 --> 00:27:28,335
-[chuckles nervously]
-I'm sorry.

418
00:27:30,504 --> 00:27:33,757
At first, I thought you were
the guy she was seeing.

419
00:27:33,883 --> 00:27:39,388
Your fancy suit, the watch and shoes,
they are exactly like his.

420
00:27:39,513 --> 00:27:41,807
-[scoffs]
-Turns out that you're a bigger deal.

421
00:27:41,932 --> 00:27:43,601
All right, just tell me what you want.

422
00:27:43,726 --> 00:27:45,478
Let's start with an apology.

423
00:27:47,521 --> 00:27:49,273
-[sighs]
-[music concludes]

424
00:27:50,107 --> 00:27:52,651
I shouldn't have smashed your phone
on the ground.

425
00:27:52,776 --> 00:27:54,904
Not that. Come on, try harder.

426
00:27:55,029 --> 00:27:58,866
Uh… Is this about your family and your ex?

427
00:27:58,991 --> 00:28:02,661
Yes. You said
he was a piece of shit, right?

428
00:28:02,786 --> 00:28:04,830
He's a good person.
You had no right to say that.

429
00:28:04,955 --> 00:28:05,873
[scoffs]

430
00:28:07,249 --> 00:28:11,003
-You're not together, are you?
-He doesn't deserve your disrespect.

431
00:28:11,670 --> 00:28:14,715
Wow. True love.

432
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:17,426
Still so affectionate
even after the breakup.

433
00:28:17,551 --> 00:28:18,719
-All right, I apologize.
-[exhales]

434
00:28:18,844 --> 00:28:22,431
Now, stop acting like a child
and tell me what you want.

435
00:28:22,556 --> 00:28:24,308
Double my directing fee.

436
00:28:24,850 --> 00:28:26,477
-[intriguing music playing]
-[scoffs]

437
00:28:26,602 --> 00:28:28,187
[Mi-do] A co-director credit.

438
00:28:28,312 --> 00:28:30,648
Fifty percent ownership of the IP.

439
00:28:30,773 --> 00:28:33,692
Ah, and articles regarding my resignation

440
00:28:33,817 --> 00:28:36,237
will have to go through me
before they're released.

441
00:28:37,321 --> 00:28:39,740
A week should be enough time.

442
00:28:46,205 --> 00:28:47,623
[music concludes]

443
00:28:47,748 --> 00:28:48,791
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY R&D CENTER

444
00:28:48,916 --> 00:28:49,750
Hey, Sang-hun.

445
00:28:49,875 --> 00:28:52,670
I'm at Incheon Research Center
for a department meeting.

446
00:28:53,504 --> 00:28:58,217
The consumer feedback survey
compared to the sensory test…

447
00:28:58,342 --> 00:29:00,302
Hey, can we talk for a minute? Huh?

448
00:29:01,011 --> 00:29:03,806
I… I can't be the only one who thinks
that we have a thing, right?

449
00:29:05,057 --> 00:29:08,185
[Su-a] It was only a business lunch.
Don't read too much into it.

450
00:29:09,061 --> 00:29:11,021
You… You call that a business lunch?

451
00:29:11,146 --> 00:29:12,189
Yeah.

452
00:29:13,148 --> 00:29:14,525
[Yeon-ho]
You asked me out on a Friday night

453
00:29:14,650 --> 00:29:17,152
because you wanted to hear
about grub infestations

454
00:29:17,278 --> 00:29:19,238
-in the sweet potato fields?
-Yeah.

455
00:29:19,989 --> 00:29:20,864
[scoffs]

456
00:29:20,990 --> 00:29:24,451
Since we mainly use sweet potatoes,
I needed to study them thoroughly.

457
00:29:24,577 --> 00:29:27,746
And because you handle the production,
I thought I needed your opinion.

458
00:29:27,871 --> 00:29:30,416
Who asks for a professional opinion
on a Friday night?

459
00:29:31,625 --> 00:29:32,626
[sighs]

460
00:29:37,006 --> 00:29:39,091
Look, I have no personal interest.

461
00:29:40,092 --> 00:29:42,303
Don't reach out
unless it's work-related, okay?

462
00:29:42,428 --> 00:29:43,596
Uh…

463
00:29:46,432 --> 00:29:49,268
Oh, God damn it. [sighs]

464
00:29:49,393 --> 00:29:51,687
-[footsteps receding]
-[door opens]

465
00:29:51,812 --> 00:29:53,480
-[Su-a sighs]
-[door closes]

466
00:29:55,816 --> 00:29:58,068
[footsteps approaching]

467
00:29:58,193 --> 00:29:59,778
[Su-a] Can I have a smoke, please?

468
00:30:02,239 --> 00:30:03,490
These are kind of strong.

469
00:30:03,616 --> 00:30:06,243
I smoke those. Raven Blue.

470
00:30:08,245 --> 00:30:11,707
The guy who taught me to smoke
in high school liked that brand.

471
00:30:17,588 --> 00:30:21,050
Sounds like a punk.
Giving this crap to a high school kid.

472
00:30:21,967 --> 00:30:23,302
Let's head to the meeting now.

473
00:30:25,304 --> 00:30:27,181
-[footsteps receding]
-[scoffs]

474
00:30:28,390 --> 00:30:29,725
[intriguing music playing]

475
00:30:29,850 --> 00:30:32,770
What is the point of switching
from perilla to sesame in  goguma  chips?

476
00:30:32,895 --> 00:30:34,021
Remind me.

477
00:30:35,022 --> 00:30:38,192
Well, whether we like it or not,
we need to change the ingredient.

478
00:30:39,026 --> 00:30:41,362
The monsoon wiped out
the perilla crops last season,

479
00:30:41,487 --> 00:30:43,405
so we don't have any other choice.

480
00:30:44,490 --> 00:30:47,368
Besides, the research team
approved using sesame instead.

481
00:30:49,662 --> 00:30:50,954
[Su-a] The board meeting's in two days.

482
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:54,458
-There's no time for tasting.
-[laughs]

483
00:30:56,669 --> 00:31:00,589
Let's get everyone else's opinion.
Uh, are you all on board with the change?

484
00:31:03,384 --> 00:31:06,637
-[employee 1] I can't really tell.
-It tastes the same, honestly.

485
00:31:06,762 --> 00:31:08,180
-[employee 2] It's not bad at all, yeah.
-Yeah.

486
00:31:10,349 --> 00:31:14,937
You see? Su-a, the consumers
won't even be able to tell the difference.

487
00:31:15,062 --> 00:31:16,271
Let's move on.

488
00:31:17,648 --> 00:31:19,983
[Namgung] Well, there's definitely
an acidic aftertaste.

489
00:31:20,109 --> 00:31:21,360
[music fades]

490
00:31:21,485 --> 00:31:25,280
Sesame has a high unsaturated fat content.
It spoils faster.

491
00:31:26,115 --> 00:31:28,492
Which leaves a bad aftertaste,
if you ask me.

492
00:31:28,617 --> 00:31:30,327
-If there's an issue with ingredients…
-[sighs]

493
00:31:30,452 --> 00:31:33,247
…I believe we can talk it through
and find common ground.

494
00:31:33,372 --> 00:31:36,542
If we need to change the mix ratio,
we'll share the data

495
00:31:36,667 --> 00:31:39,461
with the purchasing department, right?
I hope you'll understand.

496
00:31:40,337 --> 00:31:44,216
Of course, that makes sense.
That's the protocol from now on.

497
00:31:45,467 --> 00:31:47,469
But we need to let it slide this time.

498
00:31:47,594 --> 00:31:49,888
We don't have time
to make a new seasoning. [sighs]

499
00:31:50,013 --> 00:31:51,557
I'll produce it, sir.

500
00:31:54,601 --> 00:31:59,022
-[quirky piano music playing]
-[cutlery clinking]

501
00:32:13,370 --> 00:32:17,458
-[sighs] All right, spit it out.
-The imported sweet potatoes.

502
00:32:17,583 --> 00:32:20,711
You reported it to Manager Yoon Jae-mun,
did you not?

503
00:32:23,297 --> 00:32:25,090
No, I did not.

504
00:32:25,215 --> 00:32:29,511
If you can't trust your direct superior,
you could have reported it to Audit.

505
00:32:33,807 --> 00:32:35,434
Too many people are involved, so…

506
00:32:36,101 --> 00:32:39,646
with no hard evidence,
like the Distribution Team bribery case,

507
00:32:40,272 --> 00:32:42,232
only a couple of pawns
would take the fall.

508
00:32:42,357 --> 00:32:45,235
[chuckles] Obviously,
it's a very dangerous case,

509
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:48,363
-and you want to drag me into it.
-I was getting lonely.

510
00:32:49,406 --> 00:32:50,491
I shouldn't have told you.

511
00:32:50,616 --> 00:32:52,618
[cutlery clinking continues]

512
00:32:55,621 --> 00:32:56,830
[Namgung sighs]

513
00:32:58,749 --> 00:32:59,708
[gasps]

514
00:33:00,501 --> 00:33:04,546
Among the people involved, is there anyone
you're personally connected to?

515
00:33:04,671 --> 00:33:09,343
Maybe a… a blood relative or, uh,
an irreconcilable family dispute,

516
00:33:09,468 --> 00:33:13,597
and you are simply in pursuit of revenge,
and that's your motivation?

517
00:33:14,681 --> 00:33:17,601
I'm truly sorry to disappoint,
but that is not my motivation.

518
00:33:19,019 --> 00:33:20,312
Huh.

519
00:33:21,814 --> 00:33:23,065
You're climbing up the ladder.

520
00:33:23,190 --> 00:33:25,609
You'd be the youngest executive
moving up ranks--

521
00:33:25,734 --> 00:33:27,444
I'm not moving up ranks.

522
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:31,907
You're doing this just because?

523
00:33:33,033 --> 00:33:34,827
That makes no sense to me.

524
00:33:34,952 --> 00:33:37,246
[inhales deeply] It's just my nature.

525
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:39,832
Hmm. I can't ignore what I've seen.

526
00:33:39,957 --> 00:33:42,835
If I latch onto a case,
I have to get to the bottom of it.

527
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:44,711
I keep digging and following every lead.

528
00:33:45,587 --> 00:33:48,048
It's not out of justice
or a sense of duty.

529
00:33:48,173 --> 00:33:52,052
-So, I'm just an awkward kind of girl.
-[music concludes]

530
00:33:54,137 --> 00:33:55,722
Okay, I get the point.

531
00:33:56,265 --> 00:33:58,892
If that's how strongly you feel,
I will respect that.

532
00:34:03,522 --> 00:34:05,399
-[sighs]
-[cutlery clinking]

533
00:34:06,483 --> 00:34:09,111
You know this is Kitchen Lab 3, right?

534
00:34:10,696 --> 00:34:14,700
Ah, you didn't know.
You shouldn't be here by yourself.

535
00:34:15,492 --> 00:34:18,662
They say this kitchen's haunted.
It's not just a rumor.

536
00:34:18,787 --> 00:34:21,498
-I saw a lot while working here.
-I don't mind.

537
00:34:22,207 --> 00:34:25,043
-I'd kick the ghost's ass.
-Oh.

538
00:34:29,464 --> 00:34:31,675
Please say hi for me if you see the ghost.

539
00:34:33,051 --> 00:34:36,138
-Ask how it's doing.
-Yeah, I will.

540
00:34:36,805 --> 00:34:37,890
[scoffs]

541
00:34:39,933 --> 00:34:42,728
-[footsteps receding]
-[door opens]

542
00:34:43,812 --> 00:34:44,897
[door closes]

543
00:34:47,900 --> 00:34:49,651
-[sighs]
-[indistinct chatter]

544
00:34:49,776 --> 00:34:53,363
[cell phone vibrating]

545
00:34:54,907 --> 00:34:55,991
Oh, hey.

546
00:34:57,743 --> 00:35:00,996
[quirky instrumental music plays, fades]

547
00:35:01,121 --> 00:35:02,414
CONTEST FOR ENGAGED COUPLES

548
00:35:02,706 --> 00:35:04,583
[laughs awkwardly]

549
00:35:04,708 --> 00:35:08,670
Well, a couples event is being hosted
at the wedding hall tonight.

550
00:35:08,795 --> 00:35:10,422
-[Wan-do] Whoo!
-[Yeong-do] And I signed you guys up.

551
00:35:10,547 --> 00:35:12,674
-[whimsical music playing]
-[chuckles] They're having contests,

552
00:35:12,799 --> 00:35:15,135
-and you two are sure to win.
-[Wan-do] You can get a prize.

553
00:35:16,136 --> 00:35:18,513
Can you believe fifth place gets ginseng?

554
00:35:18,639 --> 00:35:22,643
I mean, newlyweds,
they're tired day and night.

555
00:35:22,768 --> 00:35:25,062
When it comes to energy,
red ginseng is the safest bet.

556
00:35:25,187 --> 00:35:27,606
-Yeah, it's the money choice.
-[Yeong-do] The money choice.

557
00:35:29,775 --> 00:35:33,946
Ah, okay, okay, okay.
Fourth place, a Bellafino coffee machine.

558
00:35:34,071 --> 00:35:35,864
Its foam is just so beautiful.

559
00:35:35,989 --> 00:35:38,659
Oh, just imagine having
a delicious espresso every morning.

560
00:35:38,784 --> 00:35:40,160
Delicious. You like coffee.

561
00:35:40,285 --> 00:35:41,578
-I know you do.
-[Yeong-do] She loves it.

562
00:35:43,455 --> 00:35:47,000
Third place, Humiel 20-liter dehumidifier.

563
00:35:47,125 --> 00:35:50,712
Man, during the rainy season,
you won't even know it's raining.

564
00:35:51,338 --> 00:35:52,839
So soft and dry.

565
00:35:55,092 --> 00:35:56,551
And second, Airponic Dress Care.

566
00:35:56,677 --> 00:35:59,262
You wear your shirts daily,
the collars get dirty.

567
00:35:59,388 --> 00:36:00,681
Will you wash them every day? Huh?

568
00:36:00,806 --> 00:36:02,724
-Huh? [gasps]
-[groans softly]

569
00:36:02,849 --> 00:36:07,187
-[hesitates]
-And first, the robot vacuum cleaner.

570
00:36:07,312 --> 00:36:08,689
[bell dinging sound effect]

571
00:36:08,814 --> 00:36:11,191
Top of the line
with AI navigation and mopping.

572
00:36:11,316 --> 00:36:13,193
[music builds]

573
00:36:13,318 --> 00:36:18,031
-So, what do you think?
-A robot vacuum. It does it all.

574
00:36:18,156 --> 00:36:20,242
Mobbing and self-navigation. Huh?

575
00:36:20,367 --> 00:36:21,785
-A robot vacuum.
-For real.

576
00:36:22,452 --> 00:36:24,079
[Yeong-do] We don't even need first place.

577
00:36:24,204 --> 00:36:27,499
-Just get the red ginseng, man.
-[music concludes]

578
00:36:27,624 --> 00:36:32,170
[host] Now, let's begin the one and only
amazing engaged couples event.

579
00:36:32,838 --> 00:36:34,131
Let's hear it for

580
00:36:34,256 --> 00:36:36,550
-the couples joining us today.
-["Heart Beat Supersonic" playing]

581
00:36:36,675 --> 00:36:38,176
BUSINESS COUPLE

582
00:36:38,301 --> 00:36:42,264
-[all cheering, applauding]
-Good luck! [laughs]

583
00:36:42,389 --> 00:36:45,642
-[sighs]
-We split it 50-50.

584
00:36:45,767 --> 00:36:47,811
-Don't you change your mind later.
-You too.

585
00:36:47,936 --> 00:36:49,730
[host] We have incredible prizes tonight.

586
00:36:49,855 --> 00:36:51,857
-♪ Your heart beat supersonic ♪
-[song concludes]

587
00:36:51,982 --> 00:36:53,108
TELEPATHY

588
00:36:53,233 --> 00:36:54,317
And now for the first question.

589
00:36:54,443 --> 00:36:57,946
In the morning,
what website does your boyfriend visit

590
00:36:58,071 --> 00:37:00,407
-every single day as he wakes up?
-[chuckles softly]

591
00:37:00,532 --> 00:37:01,658
I bet she knows the answer.

592
00:37:01,783 --> 00:37:04,536
-What do you think? Huh? What? Yeah.
-[host] Three, two, one.

593
00:37:04,661 --> 00:37:06,121
Now, your answers.

594
00:37:06,246 --> 00:37:08,123
BUSINESS COUPLE
TODAY'S DEALS

595
00:37:08,248 --> 00:37:10,000
-[crowd cheering, applauding]
-Oh, that's right!

596
00:37:10,125 --> 00:37:11,418
-Nice!
-That's right!

597
00:37:11,543 --> 00:37:13,295
-That's Lee! You got this, sis!
-[Wan-do] Yeah!

598
00:37:13,420 --> 00:37:17,257
What is your girlfriend's
weirdest sleeping habit?

599
00:37:17,382 --> 00:37:19,301
-[upbeat rock music playing]
-[host] Now, answers!

600
00:37:19,426 --> 00:37:21,219
DOING A FULL 360

601
00:37:21,386 --> 00:37:22,846
-[crowd cheering, applauding]
-[overlapping chatter]

602
00:37:22,971 --> 00:37:26,850
We wanna know what is
your all-time favorite karaoke song?

603
00:37:29,019 --> 00:37:30,020
Oh, yeah!

604
00:37:30,145 --> 00:37:31,438
A THOUSAND-YEAR LOVE

605
00:37:31,563 --> 00:37:33,482
-[crowd cheering, applauding]
-[overlapping chatter]

606
00:37:33,607 --> 00:37:34,483
SPEED QUIZ

607
00:37:34,608 --> 00:37:35,484
KEYWORD: BICYCLE

608
00:37:36,401 --> 00:37:38,236
I bought you this thing
for our fifth anniversary.

609
00:37:38,361 --> 00:37:40,614
We ended up having a fight
because you lost it.

610
00:37:40,739 --> 00:37:43,784
-My necklace!
-That was for our third anniversary.

611
00:37:43,909 --> 00:37:45,619
-Uh…
-Uh, when you were in second grade.

612
00:37:45,744 --> 00:37:47,746
-You broke your leg because of this.
-[gasps]

613
00:37:47,871 --> 00:37:50,207
-Every day I carry you.
-Bicycle?

614
00:37:50,332 --> 00:37:51,792
-[crowd cheering, applauding]
-Yes! Yeah.

615
00:37:51,917 --> 00:37:55,337
-Oh! Who do you hate most in the world?
-Lee Yeong-do.

616
00:37:56,254 --> 00:37:58,006
-Different term.
-A scrounger.

617
00:37:58,131 --> 00:38:00,008
-[Namgung] Other word.
-[Mi-do] A scumbag. A psychopath.

618
00:38:00,133 --> 00:38:01,676
A total jerk. A future loner!

619
00:38:01,802 --> 00:38:03,095
-Oh, my God!
-[music stops]

620
00:38:03,220 --> 00:38:04,179
[pants]

621
00:38:04,304 --> 00:38:08,266
Oh, you said, rather bite your tongue
than call him that.

622
00:38:08,391 --> 00:38:09,643
-A brother.
-[music resumes]

623
00:38:09,768 --> 00:38:10,685
KEYWORD: BROTHER

624
00:38:10,811 --> 00:38:13,063
-Yes!
-[cheers]

625
00:38:13,188 --> 00:38:15,941
-[crowd cheering, applauding]
-[both sigh]

626
00:38:16,066 --> 00:38:16,983
TELEPATHY ORIGAMI

627
00:38:17,109 --> 00:38:19,111
Fold it up, so the corner
touches the top, okay?

628
00:38:19,236 --> 00:38:20,403
-[Namgung] Right.
-Now, fold both sides

629
00:38:20,529 --> 00:38:23,073
-into a perfect triangle from the center.
-Uh-huh.

630
00:38:23,198 --> 00:38:25,200
Next, fold the top and both ends back.

631
00:38:25,325 --> 00:38:26,284
-Done.
-Okay?

632
00:38:27,035 --> 00:38:29,496
-Here.
-[gasps]

633
00:38:29,621 --> 00:38:31,123
-[music concludes]
-[host] And now it's time

634
00:38:31,248 --> 00:38:32,916
for today's most exciting game,
a heart rate test.

635
00:38:33,041 --> 00:38:34,042
1ST: BUSINESS COUPLE, 520 POINTS

636
00:38:34,167 --> 00:38:36,628
-It's called "Steal My Heart."
-[heart rate monitor beeping]

637
00:38:36,753 --> 00:38:39,256
[host] This game
can easily turn the tables

638
00:38:39,923 --> 00:38:44,845
simply because this round's
final score depends entirely

639
00:38:44,970 --> 00:38:46,847
on your combined heart rate.

640
00:38:47,639 --> 00:38:51,726
You'll look into your partner's eyes
for one full minute.

641
00:38:51,852 --> 00:38:53,645
Take your positions and…

642
00:38:53,770 --> 00:38:55,021
-[audience applauding]
-[Yeong-do] Let's go!

643
00:38:55,147 --> 00:38:57,691
-[Wan-do] You've gotta win.
-[host] Look into your partner's eyes.

644
00:38:57,816 --> 00:39:00,068
Can you feel your hearts racing?

645
00:39:00,193 --> 00:39:02,946
-They're doing it. They're doing it.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Oh!

646
00:39:03,655 --> 00:39:06,158
[host] In this game,
there's no fooling anyone.

647
00:39:06,283 --> 00:39:07,784
-[Wan-do] There we go.
-[Yeong-do] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

648
00:39:07,909 --> 00:39:09,870
-[Wan-do] You've got this!
-[host] Oh, look at those heart rates.

649
00:39:09,995 --> 00:39:11,580
-They're already rising.
-[overlapping chatter]

650
00:39:11,705 --> 00:39:13,957
[host] Those hearts
are pounding strong right now.

651
00:39:14,082 --> 00:39:15,750
[laughs] Oh.

652
00:39:16,585 --> 00:39:17,460
BUSINESS COUPLE

653
00:39:17,586 --> 00:39:18,712
-[Yeong-do] Oh, no.
-[poignant piano music playing]

654
00:39:18,837 --> 00:39:21,882
[host] Oh! Those numbers,
look at them, they're dropping.

655
00:39:22,007 --> 00:39:24,843
-Oh, no. They were overwhelmingly…
-[heart rate monitors beeping]

656
00:39:24,968 --> 00:39:26,845
…in first place just a moment ago.

657
00:39:27,596 --> 00:39:29,973
I'm not feeling the chemistry
between you two.

658
00:39:30,098 --> 00:39:33,143
[indistinct chatter]

659
00:39:44,362 --> 00:39:46,364
-[cashier] Is that all?
-Yeah.

660
00:39:47,324 --> 00:39:49,326
-[scanner beeps]
-[automated voice]  Please take your prize.

661
00:39:49,451 --> 00:39:52,287
Oh, you have a free gift, Hot Choco Chips.

662
00:39:52,412 --> 00:39:55,332
When this first came out,
everyone went crazy for it.

663
00:39:55,457 --> 00:39:58,126
Nowadays, they give them out
as free gifts.

664
00:39:58,251 --> 00:39:59,419
[scanner beeps]

665
00:40:03,173 --> 00:40:04,132
[scoffs]

666
00:40:04,925 --> 00:40:05,926
[can lid pops]

667
00:40:15,936 --> 00:40:17,729
[Mi-do]  You may not believe it,

668
00:40:17,854 --> 00:40:19,606
but there was a time
when we were like that.

669
00:40:20,649 --> 00:40:23,151
Every moment was passionate and exciting.

670
00:40:24,110 --> 00:40:26,196
And we only had eyes for each other.

671
00:40:27,822 --> 00:40:29,991
Those were the days
when our love shone the brightest.

672
00:40:30,116 --> 00:40:30,951
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

673
00:40:33,161 --> 00:40:37,123
Director Bong Joon-ho's film,  Parasite,
surpassed ten million viewers

674
00:40:37,249 --> 00:40:40,669
in just 53 days since its release,
breaking box office records…

675
00:40:40,794 --> 00:40:41,753
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

676
00:40:41,878 --> 00:40:43,255
…both domestically and internationally,

677
00:40:43,380 --> 00:40:46,549
it's proving both its cinematic quality
and mass appeal,

678
00:40:47,133 --> 00:40:49,761
breaking yet another record
in Korean cinema history.

679
00:40:49,886 --> 00:40:51,263
[fan whirring]

680
00:40:53,223 --> 00:40:55,475
[Namgung] I'll come visit you
every weekend.

681
00:40:56,142 --> 00:40:57,477
Actually, no.

682
00:40:57,602 --> 00:41:00,563
-I'll come every Friday after work.
-[Mi-do] Don't do that.

683
00:41:00,689 --> 00:41:03,650
You'll be too tired.
It's a ten-hour round trip.

684
00:41:04,734 --> 00:41:05,902
[gasps]

685
00:41:06,695 --> 00:41:11,491
-You've changed. Don't you miss me?
-I'm just saying you'll be tired.

686
00:41:12,701 --> 00:41:14,035
No, you're different now.

687
00:41:14,953 --> 00:41:17,163
When I ask you something,
you reply with a…

688
00:41:17,289 --> 00:41:18,581
-[grunts]
-[laughs]

689
00:41:18,707 --> 00:41:20,041
[Namgung] I'm serious.

690
00:41:20,166 --> 00:41:23,795
No, what do you mean? I'll just go, "Oh."

691
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:26,298
[chuckles] Seriously,
what else would I say?

692
00:41:26,423 --> 00:41:29,259
-You can go, "Mm-mm-mm."
-[gasps]

693
00:41:29,384 --> 00:41:32,512
-[Namgung] You used to do that too.
-When did I ever go like,

694
00:41:32,637 --> 00:41:34,472
"Mm-hmm." Of course not.

695
00:41:36,349 --> 00:41:37,350
[in higher pitch] "Mm-hmm."

696
00:41:37,475 --> 00:41:38,810
[in normal voice] That's you.

697
00:41:40,312 --> 00:41:43,940
-Do it again.
-Mm. Mm-hmm.

698
00:41:45,066 --> 00:41:47,193
-Again.
-[Mi-do] Okay, you need to stop.

699
00:41:47,319 --> 00:41:51,614
-All right. [chuckles]
-[giggles] You're crazy.

700
00:41:52,157 --> 00:41:53,033
[giggles]

701
00:41:53,158 --> 00:41:55,577
-[music fades]
-Hmm. The place is kind of cool.

702
00:41:55,702 --> 00:41:58,913
-The four of us are sharing a room now.
-That's a relief.

703
00:42:00,206 --> 00:42:02,417
[sighs] I miss you already.

704
00:42:03,543 --> 00:42:06,838
-How about a selfie?
-No, selfies aren't the real you.

705
00:42:07,714 --> 00:42:10,592
-Hey!
-[laughs]

706
00:42:12,093 --> 00:42:15,680
-[groans] I can't wait until the weekend.
-Mm. [chuckles softly]

707
00:42:15,805 --> 00:42:17,932
-Uh--
-By working hard.

708
00:42:18,641 --> 00:42:20,852
-[chuckles]
-I'll call you later.

709
00:42:20,977 --> 00:42:23,271
-[cell phone beeps]
-Are you allowed to call your girlfriend

710
00:42:23,396 --> 00:42:25,565
while waiting for the potatoes?

711
00:42:26,566 --> 00:42:30,070
I'm sorry, sir.
I've already finished the seasoning.

712
00:42:30,612 --> 00:42:32,280
Once the potatoes arrive,
I just need to mix them.

713
00:42:32,405 --> 00:42:34,824
-Hmm. Okay.
-Hmm.

714
00:42:35,367 --> 00:42:38,703
-[footsteps receding]
-[breathes deeply]

715
00:42:40,997 --> 00:42:42,457
-[thunder rumbling]
-[rain pattering]

716
00:42:42,582 --> 00:42:43,666
[groans]

717
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:48,213
[sighs]

718
00:42:51,508 --> 00:42:52,425
[groans]

719
00:42:55,678 --> 00:42:58,056
[groans]

720
00:42:59,849 --> 00:43:01,518
-Oh!
-[eerie music playing]

721
00:43:01,643 --> 00:43:04,813
[gasps, yelps]

722
00:43:10,735 --> 00:43:12,028
[thunder rumbling continues]

723
00:43:18,076 --> 00:43:20,912
-[rattling]
-[thunder rumbles]

724
00:43:22,539 --> 00:43:24,124
-[Namgung gasps softly]
-[music intensifies]

725
00:43:25,125 --> 00:43:26,126
Spooky.

726
00:43:29,462 --> 00:43:31,756
-[gasps, exclaims]
-[eerie musical sting]

727
00:43:34,259 --> 00:43:36,469
[music fades]

728
00:43:36,594 --> 00:43:42,142
Namgung! [giggles]

729
00:43:42,684 --> 00:43:45,895
-[thunder rumbling]
-[giggles]

730
00:43:49,732 --> 00:43:55,113
What? Why are you just standing there?
[gasps] Are you happy?

731
00:43:55,238 --> 00:43:58,658
Hmm? Hmm? Mm-hmm. [giggles]

732
00:43:58,783 --> 00:44:03,246
-Why are you here? And the shoot?
-The rain forced us to cancel.

733
00:44:03,371 --> 00:44:05,331
I caught a ride
with the staff heading to Incheon.

734
00:44:06,583 --> 00:44:08,626
-But how did you get in here?
-[chuckles]

735
00:44:10,128 --> 00:44:14,048
Ta-da. I spooked this guy away. [giggles]

736
00:44:15,800 --> 00:44:16,759
[exhales sharply]

737
00:44:16,885 --> 00:44:18,887
We were short on extras today.
We had to fill in.

738
00:44:19,012 --> 00:44:22,432
That's why I look like this.
Hmm? Hmm? Hmm.

739
00:44:23,933 --> 00:44:27,395
[groans] What's with this boring reaction?

740
00:44:28,730 --> 00:44:34,861
Should I just leave? Hmm.
I'll go now. I'm gonna go. Hmm?

741
00:44:36,070 --> 00:44:37,947
[sighs] You're so mean.

742
00:44:41,493 --> 00:44:42,494
I'm gonna kill you.

743
00:44:44,204 --> 00:44:46,080
You almost gave me
a heart attack a minute ago.

744
00:44:46,206 --> 00:44:47,499
Never again.

745
00:44:48,291 --> 00:44:51,794
Your reaction was so underwhelming
that it's not allowed anymore.

746
00:44:54,422 --> 00:44:55,465
I'm gonna get you.

747
00:44:56,883 --> 00:45:01,429
What kind of boring welcome was that?
Hmm? Such a buzzkill.

748
00:45:01,554 --> 00:45:04,599
[inhales sharply] You actually need
to react so that I can--

749
00:45:07,060 --> 00:45:09,270
[passionate guitar music playing]

750
00:45:18,655 --> 00:45:21,824
[Mi-do moans softly]

751
00:45:21,950 --> 00:45:23,618
[Namgung breathes sharply]

752
00:45:23,743 --> 00:45:25,703
[objects clattering]

753
00:45:25,828 --> 00:45:28,831
[both moan softly]

754
00:45:35,505 --> 00:45:39,676
-[Mi-do moans softly]
-[objects clattering]

755
00:45:40,969 --> 00:45:43,596
-[Mi-do moans softly]
-[bowl clattering]

756
00:45:43,721 --> 00:45:46,766
-[both moan softly]
-[music stops]

757
00:45:48,268 --> 00:45:50,436
[quirky upbeat music playing]

758
00:45:50,562 --> 00:45:51,938
-What do we do? Who is that?
-Here, here.

759
00:45:52,063 --> 00:45:53,940
[rattling]

760
00:45:55,316 --> 00:45:58,695
-Oh, sir, I thought you were gone.
-Uh… [hesitates]

761
00:45:58,820 --> 00:45:59,862
Yeah, I was, but…

762
00:46:00,613 --> 00:46:02,407
-let's just leave together, hmm?
-[music fades]

763
00:46:02,532 --> 00:46:04,909
-Hurry, let's just clock out.
-Uh, no, wait.

764
00:46:05,493 --> 00:46:07,453
-Sir, I'm not finished mixing yet.
-Huh?

765
00:46:07,579 --> 00:46:09,455
-What? Oh, jeez…
-[chuckles nervously]

766
00:46:09,581 --> 00:46:11,082
…you should have finished
that mix hours ago.

767
00:46:11,207 --> 00:46:12,208
Uh…

768
00:46:13,001 --> 00:46:14,419
[Ho-sik] Wait. Hmm?

769
00:46:15,336 --> 00:46:17,046
Why is your mix that color?

770
00:46:17,171 --> 00:46:18,006
Hmm?

771
00:46:19,048 --> 00:46:24,220
What? Is that dark chocolate
with capsaicin in the container there?

772
00:46:24,345 --> 00:46:27,724
Uh, yeah. Uh, when I tasted that,
it lacked character,

773
00:46:27,849 --> 00:46:30,643
-but I tried with…
-[Ho-sik] Oh, wow.

774
00:46:30,768 --> 00:46:34,522
That mix of dark chocolate
and capsaicin is quite interesting.

775
00:46:34,647 --> 00:46:38,151
-Oh. Mm. It's pretty good.
-Huh?

776
00:46:38,276 --> 00:46:41,738
[Ho-sik] Very impressive.
Mm-hmm. It's intriguing.

777
00:46:43,239 --> 00:46:48,161
Here, try it. Wow, it's like…
It goes really well with the spiciness.

778
00:46:48,286 --> 00:46:50,747
It's like the sweetness
wraps around the heat.

779
00:46:50,872 --> 00:46:51,956
-[object clatters]
-[Ho-sik] Mm-hmm.

780
00:46:52,081 --> 00:46:54,167
-[quirky music playing]
-[thunder rumbling]

781
00:46:54,292 --> 00:46:57,295
[eerie music overlapping]

782
00:46:57,420 --> 00:46:58,838
What… Who is she?

783
00:46:59,922 --> 00:47:03,635
-Who? Where?
-That girl right there.

784
00:47:04,886 --> 00:47:07,180
She's by the window.

785
00:47:07,305 --> 00:47:13,478
-She's v… very well-dressed, but…
-By the window? Where, sir?

786
00:47:13,603 --> 00:47:16,272
-Can't-- I mean…
-You see her? Right there.

787
00:47:16,397 --> 00:47:20,234
Her blouse is like, uh…
She's wearing a black skirt and long hair.

788
00:47:20,360 --> 00:47:24,906
-Oh. Sorry, sir. I don't see anyone.
-[Ho-sik] What do you mean you can't?

789
00:47:25,031 --> 00:47:27,950
-Who… Now, she's starting to smile.
-[music intensifies]

790
00:47:28,076 --> 00:47:30,411
-Look, she's smiling.
-[thunder rumbling]

791
00:47:31,788 --> 00:47:34,290
[yells] Oh, God, I… I'm leaving.

792
00:47:34,415 --> 00:47:36,334
[whimpers] I'm gonna…

793
00:47:36,459 --> 00:47:40,004
-[whimpers]
-[imitates ghost moaning]

794
00:47:40,129 --> 00:47:44,425
-[Ho-sik screaming]
-[music fades]

795
00:47:44,550 --> 00:47:46,719
-[whispers] He's gonna be okay.
-[Ho-sik screaming fades]

796
00:47:46,844 --> 00:47:50,098
Believe it or not, he's the strongest mind
in the company.

797
00:47:50,223 --> 00:47:51,849
-Mi-do, try this.
-[Mi-do] Huh?

798
00:47:56,896 --> 00:48:00,191
-Mm. Wow. Amazing. [munches]
-Like it?

799
00:48:00,316 --> 00:48:02,568
-Mm-hmm. I kind of love it.
-[Namgung chuckles softly]

800
00:48:02,694 --> 00:48:06,280
Wow, it's really good. [munches] Mm.

801
00:48:11,744 --> 00:48:12,578
What?

802
00:48:13,454 --> 00:48:17,041
-Why did you cry today?
-Hmm? I didn't cry.

803
00:48:18,126 --> 00:48:20,461
Come on. Why did you cry?

804
00:48:22,004 --> 00:48:26,008
[groans] What do you mean?
Hmm. It rained, so the shoot got canceled.

805
00:48:26,134 --> 00:48:28,845
I'm quite happy and really excited
to see you tonight.

806
00:48:32,432 --> 00:48:35,601
Why did you cry? Tell me.

807
00:48:36,310 --> 00:48:42,650
[breathes heavily, sobs]

808
00:48:43,985 --> 00:48:46,654
-[sentimental piano music playing]
-[sobs]

809
00:48:46,779 --> 00:48:49,490
The assistant director is so mean.

810
00:48:49,615 --> 00:48:52,493
-He's always doing that to the crew…
-What?

811
00:48:52,618 --> 00:48:54,787
-[Mi-do sniffles]
-Somebody has to stop that guy.

812
00:48:54,912 --> 00:48:56,164
-[Mi-do sobs]
-And then?

813
00:48:56,289 --> 00:49:01,919
So, he pinned the blame on me
because things weren't ready. [sobs]

814
00:49:02,044 --> 00:49:04,338
You should have pushed back.
It wasn't your fault.

815
00:49:04,464 --> 00:49:06,382
If you quit now,
you'll only prove that guy right.

816
00:49:06,507 --> 00:49:07,675
[sobs] What can I do?

817
00:49:07,800 --> 00:49:11,721
He's so rude and he's always
raising his voice to everyone.

818
00:49:11,846 --> 00:49:13,222
-[sighs]
-[Mi-do sobs]

819
00:49:13,347 --> 00:49:14,682
[Namgung] Is that jerk on set now?

820
00:49:14,807 --> 00:49:15,808
-I'll get him.
-[sobs] No!

821
00:49:15,933 --> 00:49:20,229
No, if you do that,
I'll die of embarrassment. [sobs]

822
00:49:20,354 --> 00:49:22,982
Listen, if I cause a scene,
I know you'll look dumb.

823
00:49:23,107 --> 00:49:25,234
-[sobs]
-But staying quiet

824
00:49:25,359 --> 00:49:28,571
-makes you look dumb too.
-[sobs]

825
00:49:28,696 --> 00:49:32,533
Even if you decide to quit,
they should know what you think.

826
00:49:33,534 --> 00:49:35,411
[whimpers]

827
00:49:35,536 --> 00:49:38,372
Running away like this
isn't the Mi-do I know.

828
00:49:38,498 --> 00:49:42,210
-[sobs]
-Let's go. Together.

829
00:49:42,335 --> 00:49:46,088
[cries]

830
00:49:46,214 --> 00:49:48,299
-[music fades]
-[sighs] What do we do now?

831
00:49:48,424 --> 00:49:50,927
-We can't get 500 people by tomorrow.
-[indistinct chatter]

832
00:49:51,052 --> 00:49:53,262
It overlaps with  Sonata of the Wind.

833
00:49:54,388 --> 00:49:58,601
[sighs] The schedule plainly showed
that the shoot was on the 28th.

834
00:49:59,268 --> 00:50:02,355
That was the old schedule,
but it was reworked.

835
00:50:02,480 --> 00:50:04,899
-Excuse me?
-Um, no, wait, I think so.

836
00:50:05,024 --> 00:50:07,652
-I'm pretty sure that's right.
-[Mi-do] Did you mess up again?

837
00:50:10,404 --> 00:50:12,490
-[Seung-ho] You again?
-What now?

838
00:50:13,157 --> 00:50:15,034
There's no staff left for you to blame.

839
00:50:17,411 --> 00:50:20,957
But don't worry.
I'm not here to tell the rest of the crew

840
00:50:21,082 --> 00:50:24,585
you ordered the set torn down
and screwed the schedule.

841
00:50:25,253 --> 00:50:29,090
[hesitates] Who the hell asked you?
You fucking crazy?

842
00:50:30,258 --> 00:50:33,845
Let me tell you what,
you'll never debut as a director.

843
00:50:35,137 --> 00:50:37,014
I've seen that short film of yours.

844
00:50:37,139 --> 00:50:39,725
I finally understood
why you act like that.

845
00:50:40,643 --> 00:50:41,644
[sighs]

846
00:50:41,769 --> 00:50:46,732
You're consumed by an inferiority complex.
Last thing I want is to be like you.

847
00:50:46,858 --> 00:50:50,528
Stealing angles and storyboards
and losing your identity.

848
00:50:51,487 --> 00:50:54,782
I won't end up
a has-been chasing movie premieres.

849
00:50:57,118 --> 00:51:00,913
I owe you. Thanks to you,
I know I'll be a great director one day.

850
00:51:03,541 --> 00:51:06,085
Hey, did you hear what she just said?
How dare you talk like that?

851
00:51:06,210 --> 00:51:07,920
-[crew member] Whoa! Sir, sir, sir, sir!
-I'm not--

852
00:51:08,045 --> 00:51:09,255
-She insulted me!
-[overlapping chatter]

853
00:51:09,380 --> 00:51:13,175
Hey, you! You're a nobody, bitch!
You'll never make it! You're nothing!

854
00:51:17,722 --> 00:51:21,851
It was an amazing honor, sir.
Thanks for the opportunity.

855
00:51:24,437 --> 00:51:27,148
[sighs] Five hundred.

856
00:51:28,941 --> 00:51:33,112
-Huh?
-If you gather 500 extras by tomorrow,

857
00:51:33,237 --> 00:51:36,407
I'll appoint you my assistant director.

858
00:51:38,451 --> 00:51:40,578
So, can you do it?

859
00:51:42,163 --> 00:51:43,456
[gasps softly]

860
00:51:44,707 --> 00:51:47,209
-[walkie-talkie beeps]
-[Gyeong-su] Get ready.

861
00:51:47,335 --> 00:51:48,920
-Action!
-[crew member] Rolling!

862
00:51:50,171 --> 00:51:52,882
[tense dramatic music playing]

863
00:51:57,720 --> 00:52:00,431
-[explosion]
-[indistinct shouting, clamoring]

864
00:52:00,556 --> 00:52:02,975
-[gunfire]
-[explosions]

865
00:52:11,442 --> 00:52:17,615
-[gunfire continues]
-[indistinct shouting, clamoring]

866
00:52:35,967 --> 00:52:39,261
-[music fades]
-[indistinct clamoring continues faintly]

867
00:52:40,054 --> 00:52:41,305
How did you know?

868
00:52:41,430 --> 00:52:43,849
[gunfire continues faintly]

869
00:52:43,975 --> 00:52:47,061
-You've known since we were young.
-[explosion]

870
00:52:47,186 --> 00:52:48,771
You can always tell when I cry.

871
00:52:50,773 --> 00:52:55,861
Not even my own mom could tell.
And you always know.

872
00:52:57,947 --> 00:52:58,990
Honestly…

873
00:53:01,200 --> 00:53:03,494
-I just know.
-[chuckles softly]

874
00:53:06,163 --> 00:53:07,415
I'm good at telling…

875
00:53:08,958 --> 00:53:10,459
when you're suffering.

876
00:53:13,087 --> 00:53:14,672
[breathes deeply]

877
00:53:14,797 --> 00:53:18,259
-[explosions, gunfire continue faintly]
-[indistinct clamoring continues faintly]

878
00:53:18,926 --> 00:53:22,805
Yes, and cut, and cut.

879
00:53:25,516 --> 00:53:26,767
What are those two doing?

880
00:53:28,436 --> 00:53:29,353
Huh?

881
00:53:29,937 --> 00:53:32,481
[indistinct clamoring, screaming]

882
00:53:38,029 --> 00:53:41,907
-[gentle guitar music playing]
-[vocalist singing in Korean]

883
00:53:42,033 --> 00:53:45,286
Hey! Lee Mi-do! Cut! Stop!

884
00:53:45,411 --> 00:53:49,874
[grunts] These fucking kids!
Huh? Oh, no, cut!

885
00:53:49,999 --> 00:53:53,878
Cut! I said cut! Cut now! Hey! Cut! Cut!

886
00:53:54,003 --> 00:53:55,671
Why are those two idiots still there?

887
00:53:55,796 --> 00:53:57,798
-Huh? Get out of my way!
-[crew member] Sir, please!

888
00:53:57,923 --> 00:53:59,258
[Gyeong-su] Hey! No! Fuck!

889
00:53:59,383 --> 00:54:01,677
Why are you stopping me?
They're in danger!

890
00:54:01,802 --> 00:54:03,137
[continues shouting indistinctly]

891
00:54:03,262 --> 00:54:06,265
…get them out
before the whole set goes and blows up!

892
00:54:08,934 --> 00:54:12,438
[Mi-do]  Our movie ended up
becoming the biggest hit of the year.

893
00:54:12,563 --> 00:54:13,522
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

894
00:54:13,647 --> 00:54:15,357
Today, Oh Gyeong-su's
When That Day Comes

895
00:54:15,483 --> 00:54:17,818
officially crossed the ten million mark,

896
00:54:17,943 --> 00:54:20,613
becoming the highest-grossing film
of the year.

897
00:54:20,738 --> 00:54:22,364
[indistinct chatter]

898
00:54:22,490 --> 00:54:25,117
[Mi-do]  The snack we created was
eventually launched as Hot Choco Chips…

899
00:54:25,242 --> 00:54:26,327
HOT CHOCO CHIPS SOLD OUT

900
00:54:26,452 --> 00:54:30,998
…and sold out almost instantly,
triggering a massive shortage.

901
00:54:31,123 --> 00:54:33,959
It made 30 billion won
in only three months.

902
00:54:34,627 --> 00:54:37,046
Hunmin Confectionery's stock price
skyrocketed that year.

903
00:54:37,171 --> 00:54:38,255
HOT CHOCO CHIPS SOLD OUT

904
00:54:39,548 --> 00:54:41,926
[Mi-do]  And our love was taking flight

905
00:54:42,051 --> 00:54:44,345
into worlds beyond imagination.

906
00:54:44,929 --> 00:54:49,433
[both pant]

907
00:54:56,565 --> 00:54:58,818
[both smooching]

908
00:55:00,111 --> 00:55:01,362
[clears throat]

909
00:55:02,404 --> 00:55:03,906
-[coughs, clears throat]
-[giggles softly]

910
00:55:04,031 --> 00:55:06,951
-[pan sizzling]
-[both smooch]

911
00:55:07,076 --> 00:55:08,077
[cutlery clinking]

912
00:55:08,202 --> 00:55:12,081
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

913
00:55:33,269 --> 00:55:35,980
[music fades]

914
00:55:36,105 --> 00:55:39,108
[Mi-do]  Where did all that passion
we once shared go?

915
00:55:39,233 --> 00:55:42,444
And the butterflies,
where did they fly away to?

916
00:55:43,487 --> 00:55:45,447
Where did we lose our way?

917
00:55:45,573 --> 00:55:46,949
[sighs]

918
00:55:48,617 --> 00:55:49,660
[sighs]

919
00:55:59,170 --> 00:56:01,463
[pants]

920
00:56:01,589 --> 00:56:03,632
-[sign beeping]
-[footsteps running]

921
00:56:09,221 --> 00:56:11,473
-Oh!
-[car horn honking]

922
00:56:11,599 --> 00:56:15,227
-[gasps, breathes heavily]
-[car horn honking]

923
00:56:15,853 --> 00:56:21,859
-[grunts, gasps]
-[car horns honking]

924
00:56:30,284 --> 00:56:33,329
[breathes shakily, inhales]

925
00:56:35,414 --> 00:56:38,918
-[car horn honking]
-[grunts softly, gasps]

926
00:56:42,254 --> 00:56:44,840
[breathes heavily]

927
00:56:44,965 --> 00:56:46,175
[shouts] Have you lost it?

928
00:56:50,512 --> 00:56:54,683
[breathes deeply]

929
00:56:56,644 --> 00:56:57,811
Why did you cry today?

930
00:57:00,564 --> 00:57:01,941
Why were you crying?

931
00:57:03,484 --> 00:57:06,779
What happened this time?
Why do you always have…

932
00:57:08,572 --> 00:57:11,075
I get worried when you cry!

933
00:57:13,494 --> 00:57:14,703
[Seung-ho] Director Lee Mi-do?

934
00:57:17,915 --> 00:57:22,753
Wow, it's been a while.
I almost didn't recognize you.

935
00:57:24,505 --> 00:57:25,547
How are you?

936
00:57:27,216 --> 00:57:29,927
-Good.
-And how are you doing, Director?

937
00:57:30,052 --> 00:57:34,598
Well, you know, working a lot. Crazy busy.
Are you here for my premiere?

938
00:57:37,810 --> 00:57:39,270
THE UNINVITED GUEST

939
00:57:39,395 --> 00:57:40,896
[chuckles] I'll introduce you.

940
00:57:41,021 --> 00:57:42,648
Uh, he's our production CEO
and one of the investors.

941
00:57:42,773 --> 00:57:43,774
INFINITE RUSH
NA SEUNG-HO

942
00:57:46,068 --> 00:57:49,071
-[film investor] Hi.
-[Seung-ho] This is Director Lee Mi-do.

943
00:57:49,738 --> 00:57:50,739
I'm sure you all know her.

944
00:57:50,864 --> 00:57:52,700
After  Spring Comes Winter,
the 13th season.

945
00:57:52,825 --> 00:57:54,243
[film investor] Ah.

946
00:57:54,368 --> 00:57:56,912
-[chuckles]
-[chuckles softly]

947
00:57:58,330 --> 00:58:01,875
So, Mi-do,
funny how life comes full circle.

948
00:58:04,003 --> 00:58:08,382
Remember you once told me
that I'd never make my feature film debut?

949
00:58:09,300 --> 00:58:13,887
Turns out the one who never debuted
was actually you.

950
00:58:14,013 --> 00:58:16,098
Those words hit hard back then,

951
00:58:16,640 --> 00:58:18,892
and I'd really like
to return the favor now.

952
00:58:19,685 --> 00:58:24,606
Lee Mi-do, you're never gonna make
your feature film debut.

953
00:58:26,108 --> 00:58:29,111
You've lost momentum.
You've lost your passion.

954
00:58:29,903 --> 00:58:33,949
That's why you're gonna fade
into obscurity.

955
00:58:35,326 --> 00:58:36,410
And now…

956
00:58:37,995 --> 00:58:39,204
enjoy my film.

957
00:58:40,497 --> 00:58:43,834
[poignant instrumental music playing]

958
00:58:43,959 --> 00:58:47,421
[sniffles] Well,
that's none of your business now.

959
00:58:48,130 --> 00:58:51,091
-Just don't worry about that!
-I wish I could stop!

960
00:58:51,675 --> 00:58:54,261
-[breathes heavily]
-I don't want to care anymore!

961
00:58:56,180 --> 00:58:57,765
And yet here we are again.

962
00:58:57,890 --> 00:59:00,851
Just face it. We are done now.

963
00:59:02,061 --> 00:59:03,187
[sighs]

964
00:59:04,521 --> 00:59:05,522
Mi-do…

965
00:59:07,733 --> 00:59:08,817
let's try again.

966
00:59:09,610 --> 00:59:11,111
[sighs]

967
00:59:11,862 --> 00:59:14,948
-If we put in the effort--
-Listen to me, Namgung!

968
00:59:15,616 --> 00:59:19,870
If only I could, I'd hit the reset button,
but that's not an option.

969
00:59:19,995 --> 00:59:22,873
I wish I could go back
when you were all that I needed.

970
00:59:23,624 --> 00:59:25,542
But I can't go back, can I?

971
00:59:27,336 --> 00:59:29,797
[breathes deeply] Namgung…

972
00:59:31,924 --> 00:59:33,801
wanna know what our future looks like?

973
00:59:35,302 --> 00:59:36,804
I'll become a burden to you…

974
00:59:38,222 --> 00:59:40,057
and you'll smother me with care.

975
00:59:41,809 --> 00:59:46,146
Maybe in three,
or five, or even ten years…

976
00:59:47,147 --> 00:59:49,900
we'll keep trying to make it work.

977
00:59:51,110 --> 00:59:52,277
But, Namgung…

978
00:59:53,862 --> 00:59:57,574
in the end, we… come to hate each other.

979
00:59:59,076 --> 01:00:00,202
Maybe…

980
01:00:01,245 --> 01:00:03,580
Maybe we already do
and just haven't noticed.

981
01:00:06,834 --> 01:00:08,377
Namgung, I couldn't take it.

982
01:00:10,462 --> 01:00:15,509
I couldn't bear you hating me,
and I could never bear hating you.

983
01:00:18,762 --> 01:00:20,806
I see that future ahead.

984
01:00:20,931 --> 01:00:23,642
And I can't let us end up hurt
and trapped like that.

985
01:00:25,894 --> 01:00:26,854
Why?

986
01:00:28,981 --> 01:00:29,982
Does that scare you?

987
01:00:33,068 --> 01:00:37,239
Are you scared of that future?
Does it scare you more than losing me?

988
01:00:39,324 --> 01:00:44,329
Mm. It does. Doesn't it terrify you?

989
01:00:45,164 --> 01:00:46,123
Of course.

990
01:00:47,791 --> 01:00:49,001
I'm scared too.

991
01:00:50,711 --> 01:00:51,670
But…

992
01:00:53,380 --> 01:00:55,174
I can't just let you go.

993
01:00:56,675 --> 01:00:58,635
I can't lose you so suddenly.

994
01:01:00,053 --> 01:01:01,805
That fear brings me to my knees.

995
01:01:03,390 --> 01:01:05,142
[sighs softly]

996
01:01:05,267 --> 01:01:06,268
[Namgung] Listen, I…

997
01:01:08,353 --> 01:01:09,730
Mi-do, I…

998
01:01:12,483 --> 01:01:14,067
I'll go wherever you go.

999
01:01:14,610 --> 01:01:16,820
[sobs softly]

1000
01:01:17,988 --> 01:01:23,744
No matter where it takes us.
I choose you even if it destroys us.

1001
01:01:26,371 --> 01:01:27,789
I still wanna be with you.

1002
01:01:28,707 --> 01:01:29,833
[sighs]

1003
01:01:31,877 --> 01:01:34,505
[poignant instrumental music continues]

1004
01:01:35,589 --> 01:01:36,632
Let's get engaged.

1005
01:01:41,011 --> 01:01:43,388
-Marry me, Mi-do.
-[music fades]

1006
01:01:46,808 --> 01:01:52,105
-Please, let's get married.
-[dramatic rock music playing]

1007
01:02:13,961 --> 01:02:18,298
[vocalist singing in Korean]

1008
01:02:24,054 --> 01:02:26,890
♪ I hear your voice in the quiet night… ♪

1009
01:02:27,015 --> 01:02:28,225
THANK YOU TO CHO HAN-CHEUL, KIM DA-HUIN,
AND OH DONG-MIN

1010
01:02:28,350 --> 01:02:29,434
FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCE

1011
01:02:29,560 --> 01:02:31,228
WHEN THAT DAY COMES
MI-DO

1012
01:02:31,353 --> 01:02:35,482
[Mi-do]  Namgung,
I really wanna feel butterflies for you.

1013
01:02:35,607 --> 01:02:38,527
And I really want you
to feel them for me, too.

1014
01:02:38,652 --> 01:02:42,698
[Suk-hee] His name is Namgung.
From now on, he'll be living with us.

1015
01:02:42,823 --> 01:02:44,741
You should talk to Hoya about this.

1016
01:02:44,866 --> 01:02:46,243
[Su-a]  Nice to meet you.
I'm Park Su-a.

1017
01:02:46,368 --> 01:02:47,661
I look forward to collaborating.

1018
01:02:47,786 --> 01:02:49,246
-[gasps]
-[Namgung]  You are so much clingier

1019
01:02:49,371 --> 01:02:53,000
-than I expected.
-[Su-a]  Namgung, this is clearly wrong.

1020
01:02:53,125 --> 01:02:54,251
[Mi-do]  I looked into your background.

1021
01:02:54,376 --> 01:02:57,212
You do whatever Seo Ju-hyeok
tells you to do.

1022
01:02:57,337 --> 01:02:58,630
[Tae-seung]  So, I'm a dog?

1023
01:02:59,631 --> 01:03:02,259
[Namgung]  Hey, look at you now.

1024
01:03:03,885 --> 01:03:06,597
-♪ I'm reaching out ♪
-[music concludes]

